Enable onclite SDM632 multicore (Qualcomm MPIDR topology + GICv2 cross-IPI).

The SWEET SMP path (PSCI CPU_ON via SMC, sweet_secondary_entry, the
initCPU self-SGI handshake and the GICv2 driver) is already in the tree, but
every image boots with cpus=1 because SweetCPU::start() validates the Apple
topology rule (MPIDR Aff0 must be 0) while onclite's ADT has four Kryo 250 Gold
cores with phys_id 0..3 (Aff0 = core in cluster):

  SWEET CPU: invalid topology cpu=1 mpidr=0x1 count=4

0141:
  A) SweetCPU.cpp: ONC-aware validation under `SWEET && ONC_SWEET_4K`
     (phys_id <= 0x103, Aff0 <= 3; num_cpus <= SWEET_SMP_MAX_CPUS, which is
     already 8 from 0078); the Apple check is unchanged for other builds.
  B) SweetCPU.cpp: signalCPU() targets the requested PE on GICv2
     (GICD_SGIR CPUTargetList, pe_gic_send_ipi_cpu()) and keeps the 0b10
     self-only path for the initCPU handshake; first cross-IPI is logged.
  C) SweetCPU.cpp: per-CPU start diagnostics (phys/cluster) plus the existing
     requested/selected/limit, CPU_ON target/entry/context, PSCI rc, entered
     initCPU, came alive SGI1 OK and final N/N CPUs lines.
  D) pe_fiq.c: new pe_gic_send_ipi_cpu() with sweetgiccpuoff boot arg
     (default 0) for the GIC-400 CPU-interface number; SWEET.h:
     GICD_SGIR_TARGET_LIST().
  E) machine_routines.c: ONC-aware die-cluster-id / cluster-core-id fallbacks
     (Aff1 = cluster, Aff0 = core).
  F) start.s: skip ICC_SRE_EL2 accesses under HAS_GIC_V2 (no GICv3 system
     registers on a GIC-400; PSCI CPU_ON entry level is SoC dependent).

Boot args: cpus=4, optional sweetgiccpuoff=<n>.  Base = post-0140 CI main.
